{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"bash-oneliners","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Bash One-Liners","description":"Handy one-liners for finding files, text processing, processes, networking, archives and disk space.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Snippets"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","contributes":{"snippets":[{"language":"Shell","path":"snippets/shell.json"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"snippets/shell.json":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"{\n  \"Find big files\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bbig\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"find ${1:.} -type f -exec du -h {} + | sort -rh | head -${2:20}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"The 20 biggest files\"\n  },\n  \"Disk usage\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bdu\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"du -h --max-depth=1 ${1:.} | sort -rh | head -${2:20}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Folder sizes\"\n  },\n  \"Find by name\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bfind\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"find ${1:.} -name \\\"${2:*.log}\\\" -type f\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Find files by name\"\n  },\n  \"Find and delete\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bfinddel\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"find ${1:.} -name \\\"${2:*.tmp}\\\" -type f -mtime +${3:7} -delete\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Delete files older than N days\"\n  },\n  \"Grep recursive\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bgrep\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"grep -rn --include=\\\"${1:*.js}\\\" \\\"${2:pattern}\\\" ${3:.}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Search text in files\"\n  },\n  \"Replace in files\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bsed\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"grep -rl '${1:old}' ${2:.} | xargs sed -i 's/${1:old}/${3:new}/g'\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Replace text in files\"\n  },\n  \"Count lines\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bwc\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"find ${1:.} -name \\\"${2:*.py}\\\" | xargs wc -l | tail -1\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Lines of code\"\n  },\n  \"Top words\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"btop\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"tr -cs '[:alpha:]' '\\\\\\\\n' < ${1:file.txt} | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -${2:20}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Most frequent words\"\n  },\n  \"Unique lines\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"buniq\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"sort ${1:file.txt} | uniq -c | sort -rn\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Unique lines, counted\"\n  },\n  \"Port in use\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bport\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"lsof -i :${1:3000}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"What uses a port\"\n  },\n  \"Kill by port\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bkillport\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"kill -9 $(lsof -t -i :${1:3000})\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Kill what uses a port\"\n  },\n  \"Process search\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bps\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"ps aux | grep -i ${1:name} | grep -v grep\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Find a process\"\n  },\n  \"Public IP\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bip\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"curl -s ifconfig.me\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Your public IP\"\n  },\n  \"HTTP status\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bstatus\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\\\\\\\\n' ${1:https://example.com}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Only the HTTP status\"\n  },\n  \"Download\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bget\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"curl -L -C - -o ${1:file} ${2:https://example.com/file}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Download a file with resume\"\n  },\n  \"Tar create\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"btar\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"tar -czf ${1:archive.tar.gz} ${2:folder}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Create a tar.gz\"\n  },\n  \"Tar extract\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"buntar\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"tar -xzf ${1:archive.tar.gz} -C ${2:.}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Extract a tar.gz\"\n  },\n  \"Zip folder\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bzip\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"zip -r ${1:archive.zip} ${2:folder} -x \\\"*.git*\\\"\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Zip a folder\"\n  },\n  \"SSH key\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bsshkey\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C \\\"${1:you@example.com}\\\" -f ~/.ssh/${2:id_ed25519}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Make an ed25519 key\"\n  },\n  \"Random password\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bpass\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"openssl rand -base64 ${1:24}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A random password\"\n  },\n  \"Hash a file\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bhash\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"sha256sum ${1:file}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"SHA-256 of a file\"\n  },\n  \"Watch\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bwatch\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"watch -n ${1:2} ${2:\\\"command\\\"}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Repeat a command\"\n  },\n  \"Parallel loop\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bpar\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"ls ${1:*.png} | xargs -P ${2:4} -I{} ${3:convert {} {}.webp}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Run jobs in parallel\"\n  },\n  \"Rename extension\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bren\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"for f in *.${1:txt}; do mv \\\"$f\\\" \\\"${f%.${1:txt}}.${2:md}\\\"; done\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Rename file extensions\"\n  },\n  \"Git: big files\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bgitbig\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"git rev-list --objects --all | git cat-file --batch-check='%(objecttype) %(objectname) %(objectsize) %(rest)' | sed -n 's/^blob //p' | sort -k2 -n -r | head -${1:10}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Biggest files in git history\"\n  },\n  \"Backup with date\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bbackup\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"cp -a ${1:file} ${1:file}.$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A dated copy\"\n  },\n  \"JSON pretty\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bjq\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"curl -s ${1:https://api.example.com} | jq ${2:.}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Pretty print JSON\"\n  }\n}\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Bash One-Liners\n\nHandy one-liners for finding files, text processing, processes, networking, archives and disk space.\n\nType a prefix and press Tab. 27 snippets.\n\n| Language | Prefix | What it inserts |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Shell | `bbig` | The 20 biggest files |\n| Shell | `bdu` | Folder sizes |\n| Shell | `bfind` | Find files by name |\n| Shell | `bfinddel` | Delete files older than N days |\n| Shell | `bgrep` | Search text in files |\n| Shell | `bsed` | Replace text in files |\n| Shell | `bwc` | Lines of code |\n| Shell | `btop` | Most frequent words |\n| Shell | `buniq` | Unique lines, counted |\n| Shell | `bport` | What uses a port |\n| Shell | `bkillport` | Kill what uses a port |\n| Shell | `bps` | Find a process |\n| Shell | `bip` | Your public IP |\n| Shell | `bstatus` | Only the HTTP status |\n| Shell | `bget` | Download a file with resume |\n| Shell | `btar` | Create a tar.gz |\n| Shell | `buntar` | Extract a tar.gz |\n| Shell | `bzip` | Zip a folder |\n| Shell | `bsshkey` | Make an ed25519 key |\n| Shell | `bpass` | A random password |\n| Shell | `bhash` | SHA-256 of a file |\n| Shell | `bwatch` | Repeat a command |\n| Shell | `bpar` | Run jobs in parallel |\n| Shell | `bren` | Rename file extensions |\n| Shell | `bgitbig` | Biggest files in git history |\n| Shell | `bbackup` | A dated copy |\n| Shell | `bjq` | Pretty print JSON |\n\nThis extension runs no code and asks for no permissions.\n"}}}